msgid "cage"
msgstr "cage"

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/cage.md
msgid "The optional lifecycle section of holo, not a separate exported function. Use it to send committed input props into model actions."
msgstr "The optional lifecycle section of holo, not a separate exported function. Use it to send committed input props into model actions."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/cage.md
msgid "`onMount(get, set, ctx)`, `onChange(get, set, ctx)`, `onUnmount(get, set, ctx)` are synchronous and return nothing. Async handlers and cleanup returns are not supported. Dispatch actions from handlers; let the model own async policies."
msgstr "`onMount(get, set, ctx)`, `onChange(get, set, ctx)`, `onUnmount(get, set, ctx)` are synchronous and return nothing. Async handlers and cleanup returns are not supported. Dispatch actions from handlers; let the model own async policies."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/cage.md
msgid "For each committed instance/store, order is mount → initial change → later shallow input changes → unmount. State changes alone do not trigger onChange. `ctx.props` merges public inputs and bindProps, excludes state/actions outputs, and uses the latest committed inputs on unmount."
msgstr "For each committed instance/store, order is mount → initial change → later shallow input changes → unmount. State changes alone do not trigger onChange. `ctx.props` merges public inputs and bindProps, excludes state/actions outputs, and uses the latest committed inputs on unmount."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/cage.md
msgid "Cage uses passive React effects. StrictMode may replay mount/change/unmount; handlers must tolerate it. SSR and abandoned renders do not publish lifecycle writes. Replacing the Jotai store closes the old cage and opens a new one. Ordinary Suspense hiding does not close it; initial Suspense delays its first commit."
msgstr "Cage uses passive React effects. StrictMode may replay mount/change/unmount; handlers must tolerate it. SSR and abandoned renders do not publish lifecycle writes. Replacing the Jotai store closes the old cage and opens a new one. Ordinary Suspense hiding does not close it; initial Suspense delays its first commit."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/cage.md
msgid "**Current limit:** input props are inferred from the View's props. A lifecycle-only input must still be declared on the View, as `term` is above. There is no independent cage input schema. A cage cannot initialize data that suspends its own first render, and cannot directly access a scoped Bunshi model through ctx."
msgstr "**Current limit:** input props are inferred from the View's props. A lifecycle-only input must still be declared on the View, as `term` is above. There is no independent cage input schema. A cage cannot initialize data that suspends its own first render, and cannot directly access a scoped Bunshi model through ctx."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/cage.md
msgid "Gate-like props-to-model wiring fits beside a View binding, avoiding an extra forwarding hook. This is not an Effector Gate: no shared open/close/status object exists. Use jotai-effect for subscription-owned resources or store-wide reactive effects instead of returning cleanup from cage."
msgstr "Gate-like props-to-model wiring fits beside a View binding, avoiding an extra forwarding hook. This is not an Effector Gate: no shared open/close/status object exists. Use jotai-effect for subscription-owned resources or store-wide reactive effects instead of returning cleanup from cage."

#. Markdown. Preserve links, inline code and table/list syntax.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: docs/reference/cage.md
msgid "- [Effector useGate](https://effector.dev/en/api/effector-react/usegate/) — the props-to-model analogy; not an identical lifecycle object.\n"
"- [React useEffect](https://react.dev/reference/react/useEffect) — commit, cleanup and StrictMode constraints.\n"
"- [Jotai effect](https://jotai.org/docs/extensions/effect) — the resource ownership alternative."
msgstr "- [Effector useGate](https://effector.dev/en/api/effector-react/usegate/) — the props-to-model analogy; not an identical lifecycle object.\n"
"- [React useEffect](https://react.dev/reference/react/useEffect) — commit, cleanup and StrictMode constraints.\n"
