"- Control identity follows createModel: same definition/key/store shares a control; different keys/stores isolate forms. Default gcTime is Infinity. This retains drafts after unmount; remove them explicitly when no longer needed.\n"
"- The model exposes native register, handleSubmit, setValue, reset, setError, setFocus, subscribe, control, and other createFormControl methods. It does not fabricate useForm's formState object. Use native useFormState for flags and errors.\n"
"- Options are fixed at creation. Change values with reset/setValue and explicit model actions. This wrapper does not add reactive values/resolver prop rebinding to holo. Async defaultValues start when a holoForm root mounts, with native RHF loading state. The initial load is shared per model and is not reapplied after successful completion on later remounts. Use reset for an explicit reload.\n"
"- The factory creates no subscriptions and runs no React hooks. Custom resources still need explicit ownership. Native RHF state can be shared intentionally across stores only if the application passes the same raw control itself; createFormModel does not do that."
msgstr "- `options(initial)` returns native UseFormProps. It creates one createFormControl per model instance. `initial` is creation-only, never a reactive reset.\n"
